        example:
          "A Swedish party involved in a genuinely complex commercial dispute can still choose to represent themselves through the entire Rättegångsbalken process without ever retaining an ombud, a choice that would simply be procedurally unavailable for an equivalent dispute in Germany, France, or Spain once it crossed the relevant mandatory-representation threshold those systems impose. A party who does retain an ombud, by contrast, is making a purely practical choice about legal expertise and case management, not satisfying a procedural precondition the Rättegångsbalken itself never actually imposes.",
