        whyItMatters:
          "As with Germany, this limits how much Swedish prosecutors can simply decline politically or strategically unwelcome prosecutions as a matter of discretion, the default expectation, as in Germany, is that sufficient evidence leads to prosecution unless a specific statutory exception applies. You should place Sweden alongside Germany, rather than France, on this specific comparison, exactly as this lecture series' Spanish counterpart placed Spain, and always identify the specific statutory basis a Swedish prosecutor is actually relying on before assuming a declined case reflects ordinary discretion rather than a genuine, narrowly defined exception.",
