        example:
          "Reform proposals to change or restrict the political-party-based nämndemän nomination system have been debated in Swedish politics and legal commentary specifically because of concerns that political affiliation, rather than pure civic representativeness, currently shapes who ends up serving as a lay judge deciding real criminal cases. A case heard entirely by a professional judge, without any nämndemän at all, is possible only in narrow, specifically defined circumstances, since the standard tingsrätt criminal panel structure genuinely expects the mixed composition this concept describes as the ordinary default, not the exception.",
